description:
The single biggest finding of the canvas-7vs audit. Sequence diagrams are the only one of the six supported diagram families with a fundamentally different expected visual structure (per-participant vertical lifelines, a top-to-bottom message timeline, activation bars) -- and none of that exists anywhere in this codebase, at the parser OR renderer level.

Root cause is in the PARSER, not just the renderers: packages/diagram-core/src/dsl/sequence.ts:74-79's nextPosition() places every participant, message target, note, and block in one flat horizontal row at a fixed y=40, incrementing x by 180px per element:
  let autoPositionCounter = 0;
  function nextPosition(): { x: number; y: number } {
    const position = { x: autoPositionCounter * 180 + 40, y: 40 };
    autoPositionCounter += 1;
    return position;
  }

Neither renderer special-cases sequence diagrams either (confirmed: zero occurrences of 'sequence'/'lifeline'/'activation'/'dslFamily' anywhere in packages/diagram-core/src/render/svg-renderer.ts). So a sequence diagram currently renders through the exact same generic node-position/edge-line/dashed-container code path a flowchart uses -- visually, a row of boxes connected by lines, not a timeline. This makes loop/alt/opt/par/critical/break blocks, activate/deactivate bars, notes, box groupings, and autonumbering all effectively meaningless visually even though every one of them parses and models correctly (jmuir-dtu.4/.4.1).

notes:
All 4 user stories + polish shipped across PRs #87 (Foundational/US1/US2), #88 (US3), #89 (US4/polish, auto-merge pending). One acceptance-criteria item is blocked by environment, not code: SC-002's manual live-provider validation needs a real Anthropic call, but the dev environment's ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is rejected by Anthropic as invalid ({"error":"API key is invalid."}), confirmed live against a running dev server (2026-09-05). Needs a human to supply/rotate a working key, then: POST /diagrams/:id/chat/messages against an ERD/C4 diagram asking for a structured edit (e.g. 'give CUSTOMER a primary key attribute id of type string'), confirm a tool call fires and the resulting DSL has real ER attribute syntax. Close this bead once that passes.
SC-002 manual live-provider validation completed 2026-09-06: user supplied a new, working ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (the old one was rejected as invalid, confirmed 2026-09-05). Ran this bead's own specified acceptance test verbatim against a real Anthropic call: POST /diagrams/:id/chat/messages on a fresh ERD diagram ('CUSTOMER {}'), message 'give CUSTOMER a primary key attribute id of type string' -> setEntityAttributes tool fired (applied:true), resulting DSL: 'CUSTOMER {
  string id PK
}
' -- real ER attribute+PK syntax, not a generic labeled box. Also ran a second, independent check against UML (not in the bead's own notes, extra rigor): 'Car inherits from Vehicle... give Car a private string field called licensePlate' -> setRelationshipKind AND setClassMembers both fired -> 'Car <|-- Vehicle' + '-string licensePlate' in the resulting DSL, real UML inheritance-token and visibility-marker syntax. Both confirm User Story 2's actual requested value (type-correct structured edits via family-specific tools) holds against a real, non-mock LLM provider, not just the mock-NLU e2e suite.
